    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Penitent Host",
    "summary": "As your [Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) begins, you may pick 1 Vow of Atonement for your army; it stays active until your next [Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) begins. Each vow can be picked once per battle:\n\n- **The Path of the Penitent**: **PENITENT** models in your army get +3\" Move.\n- **Absolution in Battle**: when a unit of yours that has made a **[Charge Move](vsdata:core-rule/charge-move)** in this turn is [picked to fight](vsdata:core-rule/fight-phase), melee weapons of its **PENITENT** models get +1 Attacks and +1 Strength until the phase ends.\n- **Death Before Disgrace**: when a melee attack destroys a **PENITENT** model of yours that has not yet fought this phase, roll 1 D6. On a 2+, leave it in play: it may fight once the attacking unit finishes its attacks, then it is removed.",
